# Git commits

- **Do not create commits** unless the user explicitly asks in their prompt (e.g. “commit”, “crée un commit”).
- Never commit as a side effect of finishing a task.
- **At the end of every prompt response**, propose a short commit message in **English**, even if the user did not ask to commit:
  - Clear and plain (not overly technical)
  - 1–2 short sentences max
  - Focus on why / user-facing impact, not file lists
  - If nothing meaningful changed, say so briefly instead of inventing a fake message
- Only run `git commit` when the user explicitly requests it; use the proposed message (or their edit of it).
- Do not push unless the user explicitly asks.
